# T-1168: mu combinator tests — S-862 equirecursive-migration
# All three test cases from T-1168 are implemented in equirecursive-core/:
#   1. mu_contractive_record_body.llt-eval — contractive list type (passes)
#   2. mu_non_contractive_bare_ref.llt-eval — μa.a rejected (errors)
#   3. mu_non_contractive_union.llt-eval — μa.(a|Int) rejected (errors)
# This file verifies that expand_named is wired into the annotation resolver
# and recursive named type aliases work end-to-end at runtime.
[
  List: [type Cons: [val: Int  tail: List]  Nil]
  xs:   [List.Cons val: 1 tail: [List.Cons val: 2 tail: List.Nil]]
  r:    [match xs
    [case [let p] [List.Cons p] p.val]
    List.Nil:                   0]
]
r
=== out
Int(1)
